Summary
-------
1. Correctness: max |par - seq| stays at machine precision (1e-7 .. 1e-6)
   across all T. log Z bit-identical.  100% forward-law equivalence.

2. Convergence: DEER iters per window CONSTANT at 2 for every T tested.
   Compare to the flat per-step Gumbel PF (logs/gumbel_pf_scaling.log)
   where iters scaled linearly with T (T=1024 -> 716 iters; fails to
   converge at T>=2048).  The twist + windowing changed iter scaling
   from O(T) to O(1).

3. Wall-clock: monotonic speedup growing from 1.85x at T=128 to a
   plateau of ~3.3x for T>=4096.  Plateau is most likely set by the
   serial scan-over-windows (num_windows = T/K = T/32) becoming a
   non-trivial share of total cost.  Increasing K should push the
   plateau higher; that is the next thing to sweep.
